### `gen_ai.turn.*` / `gen_ai.step.*` `[RFC v0.4 gap closure]`

> **RFC field:** Session / Turn / Step IDs · **Tier:** MUST · **§5 Application & Agent Reasoning Core** · **Grounding attacks:** `AOC-03`, `AOC-07`, `TA-07`, `TA-08`
>
> The RFC defines a five-level identifier hierarchy: instance → run → session → turn → step. AITF already carried instance (`gen_ai.agent.id`), run (OTel `trace_id`) and session (`gen_ai.conversation.id`). The **turn** level had no attribute and the **step** level had only an ordinal (`gen_ai.agent.step.index`) with no stable identifier independent of the OTel `span_id`. These attributes close both, so a detection can point at *which turn* behaviour changed rather than only at which run.

| Attribute | Type | Requirement | Description | Mapping |
|-----------|------|-------------|-------------|---------|
| `gen_ai.turn.id` | string | **Required** | Identifier for one request→response cycle within a session. Stable across every span emitted for that turn | NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2, EU AI Act Art.12 |
| `gen_ai.turn.index` | int | **Recommended** | Zero-based ordinal of this turn within `gen_ai.conversation.id` | NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5 |
| `gen_ai.turn.parent_id` | string | **Optional** | Preceding turn identifier, where turns branch or are retried | NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2 |
| `gen_ai.step.id` | string | **Recommended** | Identifier for one action within a turn. Defaults to the OTel `span_id`; set explicitly where the framework owns step identity | NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2 |
| `gen_ai.step.parent_id` | string | **Optional** | Preceding step identifier within the turn | NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2 |
| `gen_ai.run.id` | string | **Recommended** | Workflow/run identifier where the deployment does not use the OTel `trace_id` as the run identity | NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2, EU AI Act Art.12 |

**Emission rule.** `gen_ai.conversation.id`, `gen_ai.turn.id` and `gen_ai.step.id` are span attributes, never event bodies, and all three are low-cardinality relative to content. A span that carries `gen_ai.turn.id` MUST also carry `gen_ai.conversation.id`.

### `gen_ai.trigger.*` `[RFC v0.4 gap closure]`

> **RFC field:** Trigger Type & Source Event · **Tier:** MUST · **§5 Application & Agent Reasoning Core** · **Grounding attacks:** `TA-01`, `AOC-04`, `AOC-10`, `AOC-12`
>
> Records whether a run was started by a human or by the environment, and for autonomous runs what started it. This is distinct from Surface/App, which records the channel rather than the initiator. `TA-01` is zero-click, so *"show me every autonomous run triggered by inbound email"* is the first filter of any injection hunt.

