### `mcp.tool.definition.*` [RFC v0.4 gap closure]

> **RFC field:** Tool Definition Digest · **Tier:** MUST · **RFC §:** §9 · **Grounding attacks:** AOC-11 (rug-pull tool redefinition), AOC-09 (malicious server), AOC-16 (supply-chain substitution), TA-04 · **ODIS:** `resource_indicators`

A tool's *declared contract* — its name, description, and input/output JSON Schema — is the text the model reads when deciding whether and how to call it. A server may serve a benign definition during review and a different one at call time ("rug pull"); without a digest of the definition actually in force at the moment of the call, that substitution leaves no trace. The digest MUST be computed over the **canonicalised** definition so that whitespace and key ordering do not produce spurious changes.

| Attribute | Type | Requirement | Description | Mapping |
|-----------|------|-------------|-------------|---------|
| `mcp.tool.definition.hash` | string | **Required** | SHA-256 of the canonicalised tool definition in force for this call. Canonicalisation: JSON object `{"name","description","inputSchema","outputSchema"}`, RFC 8785 JCS, UTF-8, hex-encoded digest prefixed `sha256:` | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010), [AML.T0040](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0040), OWASP LLM06 |
| `mcp.tool.definition.baseline_hash` | string | **Recommended** | Digest of the approved/reviewed definition this call was compared against | NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2, MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010) |
| `mcp.tool.definition.changed` | boolean | **Required** | Whether `hash` differs from `baseline_hash`. Emit `false` explicitly — absence is not evidence of no change | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010), OWASP LLM06 |
| `mcp.tool.definition.change_type` | string[] | **Recommended** | Which parts changed: `"name"`, `"description"`, `"input_schema"`, `"output_schema"`, `"annotations"` | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010) |
| `mcp.tool.definition.description_hash` | string | **Recommended** | Separate digest of the description alone — the field most often used to carry injected instructions | OWASP LLM01 (Prompt Injection), MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0051](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0051) |
| `mcp.tool.definition.schema_hash` | string | **Optional** | Separate digest of `inputSchema` + `outputSchema` | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010) |
| `mcp.tool.definition.approved` | boolean | **Recommended** | Whether the definition in force is on the approved list | EU AI Act Art.14 (Human Oversight), NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2 |
| `mcp.tool.definition.approved_at` | string | **Optional** | RFC 3339 timestamp of approval of the baseline | EU AI Act Art.12 (Record-Keeping) |
| `mcp.tool.definition.first_seen` | string | **Optional** | RFC 3339 timestamp this digest was first observed | NIST AI RMF MAP-1.5 |
| `mcp.tool.definition.source` | string | **Optional** | Where the definition was obtained: `"tools/list"`, `"cache"`, `"manifest"`, `"registry"` | NIST AI RMF MAP-1.5 |

**Emission rule.** `mcp.tool.definition.hash` and `.changed` MUST be present on every `mcp.tool.call` span, not only on the `tools/list` that discovered the tool. The threat is a change *between* listing and calling, so a digest recorded only at listing time does not close the gap.

