### `rag.citation.*` [RFC v0.4 gap closure]

> **RFC field:** Citations / Source Attribution · **Tier:** MUST · **RFC §:** §8 · **Grounding attacks:** AOC-13 (fabricated attribution), TA-05 (poisoned corpus), TA-11, AOC-03 · **ODIS:** `resource_indicators`

`rag.doc.*` records what was *retrieved*. Citations record what the model *claimed to have used*. The two sets are not the same, and the difference between them is the signal: a citation that resolves to no retrieved document is either a hallucinated source or an indication that content reached the generation step outside the observed retrieval path. Both are security-relevant, and neither is visible from retrieval telemetry alone.

