`identity.lifecycle.operation` records that a credential was created. It does not record what the new credential can do *relative to the one it was derived from*. Attenuation is the security property that matters: a token exchange that returns broader scope, a longer lifetime, or a wider audience than its parent is an escalation, and it is invisible unless parent and child are recorded together on the same event.

