|-----------|------|-------------|-------------|---------|
| `asset.capability.change_type` | string | **Required** | Nature of the change: `"added"`, `"removed"`, `"modified"`, `"scope_expanded"`, `"scope_reduced"`, `"reconfigured"` | OWASP LLM06 (Excessive Agency), MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010) |
| `asset.capability.set.hash` | string | **Required** | Digest of the canonicalised current capability set — the single value to alert on | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010), NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2 |
| `asset.capability.set.previous_hash` | string | **Required** | Digest of the previously observed capability set | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010) |
| `asset.capability.set.size` | int | **Recommended** | Number of capabilities in the current set | OWASP LLM06 (Excessive Agency) |
| `asset.capability.added` | string[] | **Required** | Capabilities gained (tool names, server IDs, skill IDs, scopes) | OWASP LLM06, MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010) |
| `asset.capability.removed` | string[] | **Recommended** | Capabilities lost | NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5 |
| `asset.capability.modified` | string[] | **Recommended** | Capabilities whose definition changed while retaining their name | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010), OWASP LLM06 |
| `asset.capability.category` | string[] | **Recommended** | Classes of capability affected: `"tool"`, `"mcp_server"`, `"skill"`, `"scope"`, `"data_source"`, `"model"`, `"peer_agent"` | NIST AI RMF MAP-1.5 |
| `asset.capability.risk_delta` | string | **Recommended** | Direction of risk movement: `"increased"`, `"decreased"`, `"unchanged"` | NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5, EU AI Act Art.9 |
| `asset.capability.privileged_added` | string[] | **Recommended** | Newly gained capabilities classed as privileged or destructive | OWASP LLM06 (Excessive Agency), EU AI Act Art.14 |
| `asset.capability.change_source` | string | **Required** | What caused the change: `"deployment"`, `"config"`, `"server_advertised"`, `"marketplace_update"`, `"runtime_discovery"`, `"agent_self_modification"`. `"server_advertised"` and `"agent_self_modification"` are unreviewed paths | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010), OWASP LLM06 |
| `asset.capability.change_actor` | string | **Recommended** | Principal responsible for the change | NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2, EU AI Act Art.12 |
| `asset.capability.approved` | boolean | **Required** | Whether the new capability set was reviewed and approved. `false` on an expansion is a finding | EU AI Act Art.14 (Human Oversight), NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2 |
| `asset.capability.approval_ref` | string | **Optional** | Reference to the approval record (`identity.approval.id` where applicable) | EU AI Act Art.12 (Record-Keeping) |
| `asset.capability.detected_at` | string | **Required** | RFC 3339 timestamp the change was observed | EU AI Act Art.12 |
| `asset.capability.detection_method` | string | **Optional** | How it was noticed: `"registration"`, `"periodic_scan"`, `"first_use"`, `"handshake_diff"` | NIST AI RMF MAP-1.5 |

**Emission rule (RFC Appendix D.2).** This is a state transition and MUST be emitted as an event (`asset.capability.changed`), not inferred by an analyst diffing two inventory snapshots. Snapshot diffing loses the actor, the source, and the approval status — the three fields that determine whether an expansion was legitimate.

### `asset.instrumentation.*` [RFC v0.4 gap closure]

> **RFC field:** Instrumentation Coverage / Hook Attestation · **Tier:** MUST · **RFC §:** §15 · **Grounding attacks:** AOC-01 (telemetry suppression), AOC-10, IR-01, TA-10 · **ODIS:** `attestation_method`, `runtime_instance_id`

Every other attribute in this registry answers "what happened?". These answer "would we have seen it?". Under the RFC's assume-breach posture an adversary's first move against an instrumented system is to reduce what the instrumentation sees — disable a hook, downgrade a version, drop a span processor. Absence of telemetry is then indistinguishable from absence of activity. Declaring coverage explicitly converts silence into a checkable claim: if coverage is attested at 100% and a code path emits nothing, that is a detectable contradiction rather than an assumption.

| Attribute | Type | Requirement | Description | Mapping |
|-----------|------|-------------|-------------|---------|
| `asset.instrumentation.enabled` | boolean | **Required** | Whether AITF instrumentation is active for this asset | NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5, EU AI Act Art.12 (Record-Keeping) |
| `asset.instrumentation.version` | string | **Required** | Version of the instrumentation in force. A downgrade is a coverage-reduction signal | NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2, MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010) |
| `asset.instrumentation.sdk` | string | **Recommended** | SDK/library providing instrumentation (e.g. `"aitf-python"`, `"aitf-go"`, `"otel-auto"`) | NIST AI RMF MAP-1.5 |
| `asset.instrumentation.hooks.declared` | string[] | **Required** | Hook points the instrumentation claims to cover: `"gen_ai.inference"`, `"tool.call"`, `"mcp.request"`, `"rag.retrieve"`, `"memory.write"`, `"agent.delegate"`, `"guardrail"`, `"auth"` | NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5, EU AI Act Art.12 |
| `asset.instrumentation.hooks.active` | string[] | **Required** | Hook points verified as active at runtime. The difference from `declared` is the blind spot | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010), NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5 |
| `asset.instrumentation.hooks.missing` | string[] | **Required** | Declared hooks that are not active — the enumerated blind spots | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010), NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5 |
| `asset.instrumentation.coverage_ratio` | double | **Required** | Fraction of declared hooks that are active (0.0–1.0). Any value below 1.0 bounds the confidence of every negative finding drawn from this asset's telemetry | NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5, EU AI Act Art.12 |
| `asset.instrumentation.uninstrumented_paths` | string[] | **Recommended** | Known code paths that emit no telemetry | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010) |
| `asset.instrumentation.attestation.method` | string | **Recommended** | How the coverage claim was established: `"self_declared"`, `"startup_probe"`, `"runtime_verified"`, `"signed_manifest"`, `"tee_attested"` (ODIS `attestation_method`) | NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2 |
| `asset.instrumentation.attestation.verified` | boolean | **Recommended** | Whether the claim was independently verified. Unverified means self-asserted per the provenance rule | NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2 |
| `asset.instrumentation.attestation.signature` | string | **Optional** | Signature over the coverage manifest | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010) |
| `asset.instrumentation.attestation.at` | string | **Recommended** | RFC 3339 timestamp of the coverage assessment. Stale attestation is weak attestation | EU AI Act Art.12 |
| `asset.instrumentation.tamper_detected` | boolean | **Recommended** | Whether hooks were disabled, replaced, or downgraded after startup | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010), NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5 |
| `asset.instrumentation.tamper_indicator` | string | **Optional** | What was observed: `"hook_removed"`, `"exporter_disabled"`, `"processor_replaced"`, `"version_downgrade"`, `"config_override"` | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0010](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0010) |
| `asset.instrumentation.exporter.configured` | boolean | **Optional** | Whether an exporter is configured. Instrumentation that emits into a void is functionally uninstrumented | NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5 |
| `asset.instrumentation.exporter.reachable` | boolean | **Optional** | Whether the configured collector endpoint is reachable | NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5 |
| `asset.instrumentation.dropped_spans` | int | **Optional** | Spans dropped by queue overflow or export failure since last report | NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5, EU AI Act Art.12 |

**Relationship to `observability.sequence.*`.** These two groups answer complementary questions: `asset.instrumentation.*` establishes whether a signal *would ever have been produced*, and [`observability.sequence.*`](#observabilitysequence-rfc-v04-gap-closure) establishes whether a signal that was produced *survived the journey intact*. Neither substitutes for the other; a complete telemetry-integrity position requires both.

