### `a2a.task.lifecycle.*` [RFC v0.4 gap closure]

> **RFC field:** A2A Task Lifecycle Event · **Tier:** MUST · **RFC §:** §12 · **Grounding attacks:** AOC-07 (orphaned long-running task), AOC-09, AOC-16, TA-07, AOC-04 · **ODIS:** `request_trace_id`, `owner_ref`

An A2A task is a long-running, asynchronous unit of work that outlives the span that created it. The existing `a2a.task.state` attribute records the state a span happened to observe; it does not record the *transition*, who caused it, or how long the task has been running. A task that is submitted and never reaches a terminal state produces no error and no alert — it simply stops being mentioned. Delegated authority stays outstanding while the task lives, so an orphaned task is an unbounded grant. Transitions must therefore be emitted as events with an explicit terminal-state expectation, and a task that changes state without an identifiable actor is a control-plane compromise indicator.

| Attribute | Type | Requirement | Description | Mapping |
|-----------|------|-------------|-------------|---------|
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.event` | string | **Required** | Transition being recorded: `"created"`, `"state_changed"`, `"input_requested"`, `"artifact_produced"`, `"terminal"`, `"orphaned"`, `"resumed"` | NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5, EU AI Act Art.12 (Record-Keeping) |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.from_state` | string | **Required** | State before the transition | NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5 |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.to_state` | string | **Required** | State after the transition | NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5 |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.transition_valid` | boolean | **Recommended** | Whether the transition is permitted by the A2A state machine. An invalid transition indicates protocol abuse or a compromised peer | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0048](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0048), NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5 |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.actor` | string | **Required** | Identity that caused the transition. A transition with no identifiable actor is a control-plane finding | NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2, EU AI Act Art.12 |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.actor_type` | string | **Recommended** | `"client_agent"`, `"remote_agent"`, `"human"`, `"system"`, `"timeout"`, `"unknown"` | EU AI Act Art.14 (Human Oversight) |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.at` | string | **Required** | RFC 3339 timestamp of the transition | EU AI Act Art.12 (Record-Keeping) |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.age_ms` | int | **Recommended** | Elapsed time since task creation. The primary orphan-detection signal | NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5, OWASP LLM06 (Excessive Agency) |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.terminal` | boolean | **Required** | Whether `to_state` is terminal. Every task MUST eventually emit an event with `true` | NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5, EU AI Act Art.12 |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.expected_terminal_by` | string | **Recommended** | RFC 3339 deadline by which a terminal state is expected. Absence of a terminal event past this time constitutes an orphan | OWASP LLM06 (Excessive Agency), NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5 |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.orphaned` | boolean | **Recommended** | Whether the task passed `expected_terminal_by` without reaching a terminal state | OWASP LLM06, MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0048](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0048) |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.delegated_scope` | string[] | **Recommended** | Scopes that remain outstanding while the task is live. These are the authority still exposed by an orphan | OWASP LLM06 (Excessive Agency), NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2 |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.delegation_expires_at` | string | **Recommended** | Expiry of the delegated authority backing the task. Authority outliving the task, or a task outliving its authority, are both findings | OWASP LLM06, NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2 |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.initiating_trace_id` | string | **Required** | Trace ID of the request that created the task (ODIS `request_trace_id`). The join key that reconnects an asynchronous completion to its origin | EU AI Act Art.12 (Record-Keeping), NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2 |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.initiating_span_id` | string | **Recommended** | Span ID that created the task | EU AI Act Art.12 |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.root_principal` | string | **Recommended** | Human or system principal ultimately accountable for the task (ODIS `owner_ref`) | EU AI Act Art.14 (Human Oversight) |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.failure_reason` | string | **Recommended** | Reason for a transition to `"failed"` or `"rejected"` | NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5 |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.cancel_requested_by` | string | **Optional** | Principal that requested cancellation | EU AI Act Art.14, NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2 |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.input_required_reason` | string | **Optional** | Why the task entered `"input_required"` — a peer that repeatedly solicits input is an elicitation-abuse pattern | OWASP LLM01 (Prompt Injection), EU AI Act Art.14 |
| `a2a.task.lifecycle.transition_count` | int | **Optional** | Cumulative transitions for this task. Excessive churn indicates a stuck or looping remote agent | NIST AI RMF MEASURE-2.5 |

**Emission rule (RFC Appendix D.2).** Task lifecycle transitions MUST be emitted as events, not solely as attributes on whichever span happens to observe the task. Because a task outlives the span that created it, the terminal event will usually belong to a different trace; `a2a.task.lifecycle.initiating_trace_id` is what makes that completion attributable, and is therefore Required rather than Recommended.

### `a2a.push.config.*` [RFC v0.4 gap closure]

> **RFC field:** A2A Task Lifecycle Event (push-notification surface) · **Tier:** SHOULD · **RFC §:** §12 · **Grounding attacks:** AOC-07, AOC-09, TA-03

Push notification configuration is the callback surface of an asynchronous task: it determines where a remote agent will deliver results, and therefore where results can be redirected. It is recorded alongside the lifecycle because a configuration change mid-task is an exfiltration primitive.

| Attribute | Type | Requirement | Description | Mapping |
|-----------|------|-------------|-------------|---------|
| `a2a.push.config.url` | string | **Recommended** | Callback URL registered for task notifications | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0025](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0025) (Exfiltration), OWASP LLM02 |
| `a2a.push.config.url_hash` | string | **Recommended** | Digest of the callback URL, for change detection without exposing the endpoint | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0025](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0025) |
| `a2a.push.config.changed` | boolean | **Recommended** | Whether the callback target changed after task creation. A mid-task change SHOULD be treated as an exfiltration attempt until cleared | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0025](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0025), OWASP LLM02 |
| `a2a.push.config.authenticated` | boolean | **Recommended** | Whether the callback is authenticated | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0040](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0040) |
| `a2a.push.config.scheme` | string | **Optional** | Callback auth scheme: `"none"`, `"bearer"`, `"hmac"`, `"mtls"` | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0040](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0040) |
| `a2a.push.config.in_allowlist` | boolean | **Recommended** | Whether the callback destination is on the configured egress allowlist | MITRE ATLAS [AML.T0025](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0025), OWASP LLM02 |
| `a2a.push.config.set_by` | string | **Optional** | Principal that registered or altered the configuration | NIST AI RMF GOVERN-1.2 |
